<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="rice-broc-feta" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Rice, Broccoli, and Feta Cheese Saute</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell>1 cup rice</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 cups water</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoon salt (optional)</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>2 teaspoons canola oil</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> cup olive oil</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>4 cloves garlic, minced</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 medium tomatoes, diced</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 bunch broccoli, stalks peeled and cut small (5 cups)</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> teaspoon dried oregano</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{4}</m> cup water</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>5 ounces crumbled feta cheese</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>Black pepper (optional)</cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Combine rice, water, salt, and oil in a small saucepan and bring to a boil over high heat.  Lower heat to simmer, and cook until all water is absorbed.  Remove from heat and keep covered.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          In a large skillet, heat olive oil over medium heat.  Saute garlic for 2 minutes.  Add tomatoes and saute for 2 minutes.  Add broccoli and oregano, toss well, and add remaining water.  Cover and raise heat to medium high.  Cook for 5 minutes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Stir in hot rice, feta cheese, and black pepper to taste.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>